---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="For AI agents"
  description="A predictable path to project context, the relevant UI rule, and the correct implementation source."
  eyebrow="Agent entry point"
>
  <div class="rule-callout">
    <span class="callout-icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span>
    <div>
      <strong>This design system is a draft</strong>
      <p>Do not present its guidance as approved VINASIG policy or apply it to another project without checking that project's instructions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="favicon-check-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">Required website completion check</p><h2 id="favicon-check-title">Do not forget the favicon</h2></div>
      <p>A logo in the page header does not configure the icon shown in browser tabs, bookmarks, and other browser surfaces.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="two-column-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Before closing a website task</h3>
        <ul class="usage-list">
          <li>Inspect the shared document head or layout and confirm favicon references exist.</li>
          <li>Use the official 16 × 16, 32 × 32, and 48 × 48 px exports when they are available.</li>
          <li>Check that the icon URLs account for the deployment base path and that each file is included in the output.</li>
          <li>Report a missing source icon instead of silently skipping it or drawing a substitute.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>VINASIG favicon references</h3>
        <pre class="code-panel"><code>&lt;link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/brand/favicons/favicon-16.png" /&gt;
&lt;link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/brand/favicons/favicon-32.png" /&gt;
&lt;link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="48x48" href="/brand/favicons/favicon-48.png" /&gt;</code></pre>
        <a class="text-link" href="/brand/">See the logo guide and supplied favicon files</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="dropdown-check-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">Required UI completion check</p><h2 id="dropdown-check-title">Customise the open dropdown too</h2></div>
      <p>A styled closed control is only half of a custom dropdown. The open options panel can still fall back to browser or operating-system styling.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="two-column-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Before closing a UI task</h3>
        <ul class="usage-list">
          <li>Open every select/dropdown touched by the task and inspect the actual options panel.</li>
          <li>When the design calls for custom UI, style the trigger and popup states together.</li>
          <li>Preserve visible focus, keyboard selection, Escape-to-close, and accessible selected-state announcements.</li>
          <li>Check that the popup stays attached to its control and fits on narrow screens.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Use the component specification</h3>
        <p class="card-copy">Read <code>docs/components/README.md</code> before implementing a single-select dropdown. Prefer an existing accessible component; do not ship a visual-only custom control.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/components/">View dropdown guidance and states</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">Recommended workflow</p><h2 id="workflow-title">Load context in a few deliberate steps</h2></div>
      <p>Use the narrowest source that answers the task, then check its authority and status.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="card"><p class="section-kicker">Step 01</p><h3>Read the project guide</h3><p class="card-copy">Start with the consuming website's `AGENTS.md`, then this repository's root `AGENTS.md` if the task calls for this system.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><p class="section-kicker">Step 02</p><h3>Find the matching rule</h3><p class="card-copy">Use the foundation, component, or pattern page related to the interface being changed.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><p class="section-kicker">Step 03</p><h3>Check status and source</h3><p class="card-copy">Follow approved rules when available. Mark these prototype rules as draft and keep token changes in the source file.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="consuming-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">Add to a website repository</p><h2 id="consuming-title">Keep the context close to the code</h2></div>
      <p>Each VINASIG website should identify its system version and its own approved exceptions.</p>
    </div>
    <pre class="code-panel"><code># AGENTS.md in a consuming website repository

## VINASIG interface guidance
- Design system: https://github.com/VINASIG/web-design-system
- Read the relevant foundation and component specification before editing UI.
- Confirm the version used by this website before applying a change.
- Current v0.1 guidance is draft and requires owner approval.
- Prefer tokens and components from the installed design-system package.</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">Write agent-readable rules</p><h2 id="writing-title">Make each instruction direct and traceable</h2></div>
    </div>
    <article class="card">
      <ul class="rule-list">
        <li><span class="rule-term">MUST</span><span class="rule-text">A requirement that applies whenever its stated scope is met.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rule-term">SHOULD</span><span class="rule-text">The preferred choice; document the reason when a project needs an exception.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rule-term">MAY</span><span class="rule-text">An allowed option that the implementation can choose when useful.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="card-copy">For every rule, name its scope, the source file, and its approval status. Include a small working example when a rule affects code or interaction.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="source-map-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">Source map</p><h2 id="source-map-title">Where to find the canonical information</h2></div>
    </div>
    <div class="two-column-grid">
      <article class="card"><h3>Project and agent context</h3><p class="card-copy"><code>AGENTS.md</code> · status, scope, repository map, and working instructions.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Brand identity</h3><p class="card-copy"><code>docs/brand/README.md</code> · logo variant facts, export paths, and draft usage guidance.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Design guidance</h3><p class="card-copy"><code>docs/</code> · source specifications for foundations, components, and patterns.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Implementation tokens</h3><p class="card-copy"><code>src/styles/tokens.css</code> · CSS variables and the locally hosted typeface declaration.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Published index</h3><p class="card-copy"><code>/llms.txt</code> · compact navigation map for tools that can fetch the docs site.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
